<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04JR">Variant <span data-tag="04JR">6.3.3.9</span>.</a> Let $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be a functor of $\infty $-categories. We say that $F$ is a <em>coreflective localization functor</em> if it admits a fully faithful left adjoint $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. Equivalently, $F$ is a coreflective localization functor if the opposite functor $F^{\operatorname{op}}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}^{\operatorname{op}}$ is a reflective localization functor (see Remark <a data-tag="02ER" href="/tag/02ER">6.2.1.7</a>). It follows from Proposition <a data-tag="04JL" href="/tag/04JL">6.3.3.7</a> that every coreflective localization functor is a localization functor (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="04JG" href="/tag/04JG">6.3.3.1</a>). </p>
